      <h2 id="story">Our story</h2>
      <p>[Write the real story here, in your own words. Donors read this section more closely than any other page. Cover the moment the foundation started, who was there, what the first outreach was, and why these three areas of work.]</p>
      <p>The Obaatanpa Project was founded by Madam Angela Ahimah to bring care, compassion and commitment to community development across the Amenfi East Municipality. What began as visits to elders in Wassa Akropong has grown into three standing programmes: feeding our aged, supporting the Wassa Akropong Government Hospital, and going into schools to talk with young people about health, safety and self-respect.</p>

      <h2 id="purpose">What we are for</h2>
      <p><strong>Our purpose.</strong> That no elder in Amenfi East eats alone, that our hospital is never short of what patients need, and that every young person leaves school knowing how to protect their health and their dignity.</p>
      <p><strong>What we believe.</strong> In Madam Ahimah's words: good health is a foundation for progress. Everything we do follows from that.</p>

      <h2 id="approach">How we work</h2>
      <h3>We show up in person</h3>
      <p>Donations are delivered by hand, and our team sits with the people receiving them. That is how we learn what is actually needed next.</p>
      <h3>We work with what exists</h3>
      <p>We support the hospital, the schools and the churches already serving this community rather than building anything parallel to them.</p>
      <h3>We stay local</h3>
      <p>Amenfi East is our home. We would rather do a small number of things properly here than spread thinly across the region.</p>
      <h3>We say what we did</h3>
      <p>Every outreach is reported here and on our Facebook page, with photographs and the names of the people involved, where they have agreed to be named.</p>
    </div>
